WEBVTT

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:04.170
Oops.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.230
Thank you, Nao-chan!

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:07.740
All good.

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.220
I'm opening the door.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.310
Everything's starting to turn white outside!

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.740
This snow might actually stick.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.130
Walk fast so they don't get wet.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.950
I'm nervous!

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.790
We had about this much snow last year, too.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.930
And we had a mini snow ball fight at school.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.000
Oh, right.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.050
Hime-chan?

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.940
I haven't even been in Tajimi
for a whole year yet.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.330
It feels like I've been 
here for a long time.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.000
<i>It's been two weeks since then.</i>

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.890
<i>Time to put everything into the kiln.</i>

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:02.150
This time you didn't just 
make different shapes,

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.520
you've also tried a bunch of 
different colors, too.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:08.320
Yes! I just had a lot of ideas, 
so I kind of ran with them!

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.700
I can't wait to see how the colors turn out!

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.470
Yeah!

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:15.100
All right, I'm closing it.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:15.940
Okay!

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:40.480
I'm home!

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:45.910
<b>I'm Making a Mug!</b>

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:42.380
Welcome home.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:43.440
Welcome!

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.660
Welcome home.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.930
The snow is probably going to stick.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:50.750
And it's still only December.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:55.510
Is it okay if the pottery club comes here 
tomorrow, since we're closed anyway?

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.450
Oh, sure.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.630
Great!

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:00.760
Himeno?

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.300
I might reveal the piece for the shelf then.

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:07.380
R-Really?

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:09.760
The day's finally come, Toki-kun!

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:13.020
My heart's already racing!

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:22.040
Oh, right! I have to text Ximena-san!

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:27.540
"Do you have time tomorrow afternoon?"

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:29.530
And send!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.960
Oh, Hime-chan!

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:37.550
Got it, I'll see you tomorrow then.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:45.040
Tomorrow's finally the day!

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.350
I can't wait for tomorrow!

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:55.910
It's finally time, Hime-chan! 
I'm so excited!

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:58.780
I think it'll be fine, though!

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.710
I don't know why, but I feel confident.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:02.630
You're bolder than usual.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:04.950
Did something in Hime-chan finally awaken?

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.070
What is that supposed to mean?

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:08.070
All right, I'm opening it.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.340
Yes, this!

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:35.230
The glazing sounds are even 
more magical than usual.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:38.740
The angel voices you only hear right 
after you take things out of the kiln.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.970
Maybe the angels are rejoicing that 
the colors turned out so well.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.260
Your hard work paid off, Hime-chan.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:51.370
The thing is, I don't really 
remember working hard.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:57.750
I was having so much fun and the 
next thing I knew, they were done.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.550
It sounds like you've mastered the Art of Runru.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:01.130
You're a Runru Master!

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.340
Yay!

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.880
Oh, is it already time?

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.970
I'm going to go pick up Ximena-san.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.630
Roger that.

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:13.670
All right, everyone. See you 
at the café in one hour!

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.110
All right!

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.900
<b>Closed
Today</b>

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.410
Do not peek!

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.300
Do not!

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:37.810
I want to see it already, 
but I'm also scared to see it.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:41.530
There's nothing to be scared of.

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.050
What are you talking about?

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:48.680
It's almost like the athletic 
festival back in grade school...

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:52.090
When I was filming her 
running as hard as she could,

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:56.070
I kept praying that she 
wouldn't stumble and fall.

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:59.010
You worry too much.

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:02.160
But I guess it can't be helped since 
you've only got that one cute girl.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.780
Dad, Grandma, you can come in now!

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:08.340
You can go ahead and use the counter!

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.200
Okay!

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.830
<b><i>TADA!!!!</i></b>

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.490
Oh, that's why.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.330
<b><i>TADA!!!!</i></b>

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:16.330
This certainly is an occasion.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.010
It doesn't happen every day.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.910
We're here!

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:20.850
Come on in!

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:22.360
Please take a seat at the table!

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:23.580
Did you set everything up?

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:25.420
Yup! You're right on time!

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.950
I'm here, too!

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:28.780
Don't be a bad drunk today.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:29.730
I'm not drinking today.

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:31.380
Hello!

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:34.020
Thanks for the invitation, Hime-chan!

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.980
Ximena-san! I'm glad you made it!

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:37.920
So you're Ximena-san!

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:41.710
I'm Tokikawa Himena's madre, Sachie.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:46.060
Oh, her mother! It's so nice to meet you!

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.080
All right, everybody!

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:52.830
I'll be so bold as to propose the first toast.

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:55.870
Congratulations to everyone for 
finishing the second semester!

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.520
Cheers!

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:58.830
Cheers!

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:02.620
We've got plenty of curry 
and sweets, so eat up!

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:04.090
Let's eat!

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:08.410
¡Está bien!

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:12.770
If I can have your attention!

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:15.360
Now, I know the party is in full swing,

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:18.300
but Hime-chan has an important 
announcement to make!

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:21.110
If everyone could please 
come over to the counter.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.110
Tada!

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:29.240
Go ahead, Hime-chan.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.770
We've been waiting for this!

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:35.360
It's taken me two months 
since Dad brought this up,

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:39.380
but I'm pleased to unveil the section 
for Toyokawa Himeno's masterpieces.

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:47.390
So here we go!

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:01.630
Those dishes...

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:02.820
What a surprise!

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.280
So you chose these.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.320
I didn't see that coming.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:06.280
Huh? What?

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.650
Himeno?

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:13.360
These are a Japanese dinner sets
 Ximena-san made here in Tajimi!

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:18.220
That's right! Himeno-san said she 
really wanted to display them here.

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:20.160
So that means...

00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:23.260
What does that mean?

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:33.360
This small set is for the departed.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:39.530
You don't put it on the altar, though. 
You put it on the table with you!

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:42.850
That way, the person who's gone 
doesn't have to eat alone.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:45.390
That's wonderful.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:50.360
Mom's pieces lead to this 
miraculous encounter.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.580
Hola.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:53.860
And from there, this wonderful 
Japanese dinner set was born.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:58.880
When I heard that showing things to others 
widens your horizon, I was inspired.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:02.120
Yes, I want everybody to see this!

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:05.650
I want to display it here and 
have everybody learn about it!

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:09.150
That's what I want to use this shelf for.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:11.640
Dad?

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:20.390
I see.

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.150
I see, I see.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:26.550
I wasn't expecting this.

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:29.500
But it is wonderful.

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:31.480
I'm sorry.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:38.280
You were expecting something 
made by me, right?

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:40.630
Yes.

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:48.790
You suggested the shelf because I said I needed 
a reason to come up with something.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:53.130
But because of that I unconsciously 
put myself under a ton of pressure.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:55.910
I'm sorry about that! I should 
have thought it through—

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:56.430
No!

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:05.200
Only because of that was I able to start seeing 
myself while discussing things with Touko-senpai.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:09.430
Once I decided to put these here, 
the pressure went away.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:14.180
And once I decided to make something for 
myself, all these emotions poured out.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:18.810
I felt the Runru, and it was more 
fun than I've ever had before.

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:21.210
Right! The Runru is really important!

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:25.780
And with that, here's what I made.

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:30.640
Tada!

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:32.810
So many?!

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.640
Wow.

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:39.680
As always, they're novice pieces, 
but please use them if you like.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:43.480
I kind of made one to match 
each of you without realizing.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:45.480
And this one, too.

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:48.380
Oh, is that for your madre?

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:50.180
Yup! I learned from you.

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:51.960
This one's...

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:55.070
for me.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:58.900
That's quite a simple design.

00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:02.740
Actually, that's a really complicated white.

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:03.950
Huh?

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:11.250
This technique is called "kohiki" and the 
color subtly changes the more you use it.

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:16.300
I feel like it's an expression 
of Toyokawa-san's current self.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:17.750
That's right.

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:24.250
So that's why this is my 
first present to myself.

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:27.780
Right now, I'm pure white,

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:32.010
but who knows what colors I'll become?

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:37.800
I'm hoping that I can keep 
growing alongside this mug.

00:10:40.630 --> 00:10:42.020
Dad?

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:44.490
Are you crying?

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:46.910
Silly... of course not!

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:49.290
I'm going to go wash my face.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:50.400
Dad?

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:54.710
It's fine.

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:25.270
Himena... I don't know when it 
happened, but Himeno's all grown up.

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:27.740
She used to need me so much.

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:36.370
Now, it looks like she'll be fine, 
even if I'm not entirely dependable...

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:43.970
It's good, right?

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:46.770
This is so good!

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:49.880
Nao-chan, cheers!

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:07.690
Would you like some coffee?

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:14.200
We can all use the mugs you made.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.790
Good idea!

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:17.460
Yeah!

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:22.220
Drink up!

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:33.530
Mom!

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.130
I brought her with me.

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:37.350
Yay!

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:40.440
Let's drink.

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:44.320
My mug.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:49.390
That's so good!

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:54.390
Himeno, you have a white mustache!

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:56.010
You do!

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:58.510
Well so do you both of you!

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.740
<i>Tajimi city in Gifu prefecture...</i>

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:33.810
<i>I met all sorts of people here 
and came to really love pottery.</i>

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:39.470
<i>But only now have I made it 
to the real starting line.</i>

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:43.590
<i>I have a feeling that I'll 
meet even more people</i>

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:47.560
<i>and that I will only broaden my horizons more!</i>

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:57.600
I'll be coming back here in 
April, so go easy on me.

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:06.010
I'm looking forward to that!

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:10.190
<i>I hope to find you here too, Tokikawa.</i>

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.610
<i>What should I make next?</i>

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:20.930
<i>I bet there's so many things 
I still don't know.</i>

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:25.420
<i>But I know that each thing I don't know 
will be an exciting journey for me!</i>

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:31.000
<i>My life in pottery will keep going forever!</i>

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.000
<i></i>
